# Environment variables for ledger-exception-control-plane.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# Real values belong in the environment or the platform secret store, never in this file
# and never in source control.
#
# Every variable takes the `LECP_` prefix. Unknown variables are rejected at startup rather
# than ignored, so a typo fails loudly instead of silently falling back to a default.

# --- Dependencies -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host ports published by the local Compose stack, deliberately not the service defaults:
# a developer machine commonly runs its own PostgreSQL on 5432, and pointing at it by
# default risks running migrations against an unrelated database (ADR-029).
#
# Inside the Compose network the application reaches the services by name instead
# (`postgres:5432`, `redis:6379`); docker-compose.yml sets that and these values are for
# running the application or Alembic directly on the host.
LECP_POSTGRES_DSN=postgresql://lecp:lecp_local_dev@localhost:15432/lecp
LECP_REDIS_DSN=redis://localhost:16379/0

# --- Service ------------------------------------------------------------------------
LECP_ENVIRONMENT=local
LECP_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
LECP_SERVICE_NAME=ledger-exception-control-plane

# Upper bound on each individual readiness probe, in seconds.
LECP_READINESS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=2.0

# Header carrying an inbound correlation id.
LECP_CORRELATION_ID_HEADER=X-Request-ID

# --- Cassette capture (M3.4) --------------------------------------------------------
# The switch that lets the harness record a real provider exchange. It is the only thing
# in this project that can reach a paid API, so it fails closed: unset, empty, "true" and
# "yes" all mean no, and only the exact value 1 enables capture. Recording refuses at
# construction rather than inside a send, so there is no path that records first and
# checks afterwards.
#
# CI never sets it. The committed cassettes are synthesised, the test suite replays from
# them offline, and there is no fallback from replay to a live call.
#
# **Deliberately without the LECP_ prefix**, which is the one exception in this file.
# Settings rejects unknown LECP_ names, and it rejects them from `.env` as well as from the
# environment — so writing this as LECP_CASSETTE_CAPTURE here would break startup for
# anyone who copied the example into a real `.env`. A capture switch is not application
# configuration, so it does not belong in that namespace anyway.
#
# Capture also needs a provider credential, which this repository never holds and never
# writes down: supply it to the transport you pass the recorder, in the shell, for the
# length of the run.
#
# CASSETTE_CAPTURE=1
